form.p:


(1) to denote sex, fer is prefixed to the name of an animal 

or to a nomen agentis which may be used of both sexes; 

rarely with a subst. exclusively masc. in application, 

 e.g. fermac;

 m. (Ped., ii 611, suggests a formation from frith- 

saig- through metathesis, influenced by feraid and fer ; 

forms vary).

